kitnetzday - companion code of JISAS-D-26-02300
"Towards Context-Aware Detection: Evaluating Multi-Autoencoder
Ensembles for Zero-Day Network Intrusion Detection"

This package contains code derived from third-party software. The notices
below are reproduced as their licences require. No third-party dataset is
redistributed here.


1. Kitsune-py (KitNET)
----------------------

Source:  https://github.com/ymirsky/Kitsune-py
Paper:   Y. Mirsky, T. Doitshman, Y. Elovici and A. Shabtai, "Kitsune: An
         Ensemble of Autoencoders for Online Network Intrusion Detection",
         Network and Distributed System Security Symposium (NDSS), 2018.

Two files of frozen/models/ are adapted from Kitsune-py:

  frozen/models/cluster/corrclust.py
      adapted from KitNET/corClust.py (the incremental correlation
      clustering of the feature mapper).
  frozen/models/networks/original_kitsune.py
      adapted from KitNET/dA.py (the denoising autoencoder, its online
      min-max normalisation and its train/execute interface).

In addition, frozen/runner/baselines_t5.py imports Kitsune-py unmodified,
at commit 7c8ea51e89268d9a20399dca4bf32d663e638eb4, to run the published
implementation as a baseline. Kitsune-py itself is not shipped in this
package.

The files of frozen/ are shipped without their comments. KitNET/corClust.py
carries the licence below under its own notice, "Copyright (c) 2017 Yisroel
Mirsky", and asks in a comment that the paper above be cited; both apply to
frozen/models/cluster/corrclust.py and are reproduced here.

